                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.00/254: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >McMillin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-04T21:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 4, 1919, 9
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 6, 1.06
                            a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Leguia occupied Palace during the day appointing and swearing following Cabinet:
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs and President of the Cabinet, Porras; Minister of
                    Gobernacion, Cornejo; Minister Justice, Osores; Minister War, General Abrill;
                    Minister of Finance, Idiáquez; Public Works, Gutierrez. Reported Leguia will
                    issue proclamation immediately calling for election new Congress. His present
                    determination is against designation temporary President but no steps yet taken
                    for his own induction to the Presidency. No organized opposition yet developed.
                    City tranquil.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McMillin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
